messages:
sylvia: quick flag - running into a reproducible bundler parity issue for the JS SDK in our edge sample app (vite dev -> rollup build -> miniflare). Build succeeds but worker crashes with `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'prototype')`.

omar: ouch. what import style are you using? default or named?

sylvia: `import Redwood from '@redwood/inference'` in an ESM project (`type: "module"`). minimal package.json: 
```json
{
  "type": "module",
  "dependencies": {
    "@redwood/inference": "0.12.0"
  }
}
```

jamie: likely cause: conditional exports with both import/require targets; some bundler resolvers pick the CJS path and rollup/vite/commonjs transforms produce an interop wrapper that breaks subclass/prototype checks in strict edge runtimes. can you paste package.exports from the SDK pkg?

sylvia: exports in node_modules/@redwood/inference/package.json:
```json
"exports": {
  ".": {
    "import": "./dist/esm/index.js",
    "require": "./dist/cjs/index.cjs",
    "types": "./dist/types/index.d.ts"
  }
}
```

riley: yep that's the pattern that trips older resolver versions. short-term workaround: alias explicitly to the ESM entry in vite/rollup so bundler doesn't pick the CJS file: 
```js
// vite.config.js
import { defineConfig } from 'vite'
export default defineConfig({
  resolve: {
    alias: {
      '@redwood/inference': '/node_modules/@redwood/inference/dist/esm/index.js'
    }
  }
})
```

sylvia: aliasing to ESM unblocked the worker — thanks. but this is a bad onboarding experience; our starter templates currently have no alias and new devs hit this on first run.

leo: also saw TS typing issues: `import type { Client } from '@redwood/inference'` sometimes resolves to `any` in IDEs because types are only under `exports` mapping. editors/tsserver in some configs don't follow conditional `exports.types`. Recommend adding a top-level `types` field and/or `exports.types` at the top-level that points to the ESM d.ts.

jamie: SDK action items we discussed: 1) validate `exports` shape across vite/esbuild/rollup/webpack resolvers, 2) add a `module` (or `.mjs`) ESM entry that bundlers prefer, 3) expose `types` at top-level (or in `exports.types`) so `import type` works consistently, 4) add a sample-app CI job that builds with vite/rollup and runs a miniflare smoke test.

sylvia: i'll open a sample-apps PR that adds a short README note + the vite alias snippet and include repro steps. then i'll file an SDK issue linking the repro and logs.

sdk-bot: New issue created: RED-PLAT/SDK#1833 by sylvia  "Bundler conditional-exports -> CJS picked by resolver; edge worker prototype error (vite/rollup)"

riley: also include in the repro matrix: different import forms (`default`, `* as`, `named`) and TS `import type` checks to surface both runtime and editor regressions.

sylvia: good call. PR will include three tiny code variants and a CI smoke script. I'll tag @eng-ml and @devexp on the SDK issue.

leo: when SDK fixes packaging, let's publish a tiny migration note and remove the alias from templates. we should also add a unit in sample-app CI to fail if the alias is present (so we don't forget to remove it).

jamie: agreed. thanks for triage sylvia. this will save new hires a lot of time.

sylvia: will update with PR & SDK issue links once created.
